Here is how to integrate markdown conversion into a Node.js application:

const response = await fetch('https://api.example.com/convert', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'Authorization': 'Bearer YOUR_API_KEY',
    'Content-Type': 'application/json'
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({ markdown: '# Hello World' })
});

const data = await response.json();
console.log(data.html); // <h1>Hello World</h1>

For browser-based apps, wrap this in a reusable function and handle errors gracefully. Always validate the markdown input before sending to prevent oversized payloads.
